/**
 * Reolink Source Bridge (Internal Parent Driver)
 * Version: 1.3.7-BETA3-DIAG1
 *
 * DIAGNOSTIC BUILD (2026-08-10): temporary logging added to processBuffer()
 * to chase a real bug -- the magic-header corruption pattern escalated from
 * rare/isolated (as originally documented) to firing dozens of times over
 * ~19 hours under real multi-camera load, several parse errors ago showed
 * mangled tag fragments (AItypeu/AIty/ti -- all look like AItype sliced at
 * the wrong byte offset) suggesting a genuine buffer-misalignment bug, not
 * random line noise. Prime suspect: payloadOffset is parsed from the header
 * but never actually used -- only bodyLen drives how much of the buffer
 * gets consumed per message. Now logs a warning every time those two values
 * differ, plus a raw hex dump + the previous message's header fields on
 * every magic-header failure (not gated by the 60s escalation tier, so a
 * real capture is available on the very next occurrence). No suppression
 * logic or reconnect behavior changed -- this build only adds visibility.
 *
 * BETA3: configureConnection() is no longer a manually-invokable UI command
 * (see the app's BETA3 note) -- the method is unchanged, just not exposed
 * on the Commands tab anymore, since the app always calls it programmatically.
 *
 * NOT user-facing. Created and managed automatically by the Reolink
 * Integration parent app -- ONE instance per SOURCE (Hub/NVR or standalone).
 * Users never add this manually.
 *
 * Merges two roles into one device, per Jason's refined design (2026-08-09):
 *  1. Holds the persistent Baichuan TCP event subscription (cmd_id=31) --
 *     identical code to ReolinkEventConnection.groovy / the validated
 *     ReolinkEventSubscriptionTestTool.groovy, unchanged.
 *  2. Is the PARENT that creates Camera/Doorbell devices as ITS OWN children
 *     (not the app's), via createChannelDevice()/removeChannelDevice() below
 *     -- this is what makes them nest under this bridge in the Devices list
 *     (Hubitat's expand/collapse nested UI only applies to device-owned
 *     children, never app-owned children -- confirmed from Hubitat's own
 *     docs). Same pattern as the Pentair IntelliCenter Bridge.
 *
 * Camera/Doorbell's existing parent?.componentX(...) calls now resolve to
 * THIS device (since it's their real parent) instead of the app directly --
 * every componentX() method below is a one-line passthrough forwarding to
 * this bridge's OWN parent (the app), so CameraDriver.groovy/
 * DoorbellDriver.groovy needed ZERO changes for this restructuring.
 */
